<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:21Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: FlyDubai suspends flights to and from Israel after pilot attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9e2e870477d6f47eef315e1a597d96524fb45196bada406c9bfdd41d58080f7</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T05:58:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-live-flydubai-suspends-flights-to-and-from-israel-after-pilot-attack--44a1c7b6f345.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-live-flydubai-suspends-flights-to-and-from-israel-after-pilot-attack" /><summary type="html">FlyDubai, the budget airline owned by Emirates Airlines, has temporarily suspended flights to and from Israel after one of its pilot stabbed his copilot midflight in what appears to have been an attempt to crash the Tel Aviv-bound passenger yet. Israel’s defence minister has labelled the incident as a thwarted “terror attack”. Follow our liveblog for all the latest developments.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Execution of convicted US killer Christa Pike fails despite two lethal injections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cdb55ce53848e5e62026f7f61d33322f2d8e9728dd16e7c1dbe6c43a59a3fa53</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T05:32:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261001-execution-of-convicted-us-killer-christa-pike-fails-despite-two-lethal-injections--aeb8f625e4e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261001-execution-of-convicted-us-killer-christa-pike-fails-despite-two-lethal-injections" /><summary type="html">Christa Pike, who has been on death row for more than 30 years for torturing and murdering a classmate, was on Wednesday set to be executed, but the lethal injections meant to kill her failed. Pike was then transported to a medical facility, but except for the fact that she is still alive, her lawyers said they had not been informed about her condition.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>El Salvador sets date for 2027 presidential election as Bukele seeks third term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81a205bfbfcd604c69e1e653eda719e7baf3068b2e079bed2af4c2469b17b750</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T02:32:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261001-el-salvador-sets-2027-presidential-election-as-nayib-bukele-seeks-third-term--90fb5878abea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261001-el-salvador-sets-2027-presidential-election-as-nayib-bukele-seeks-third-term" /><summary type="html">El Salvador will hold presidential elections on February 28, 2027, the electoral tribunal said Wednesday, opening the way for President Nayib Bukele to seek a third term after constitutional changes removed presidential term limits. Bukele has drawn praise for sharply reducing gang violence but faced criticism over rights abuses during his crackdown.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Russia launches major attack on Ukraine’s energy grid, causing power cuts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa953eef963361bcbfd31416de1ade2a9e3cd0f4406fe50708558d6837e2ca92</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T02:21:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-russia-launches-major-attack-on-ukraine-energy-grid-causing-power-cuts--006e908b4816.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-russia-launches-major-attack-on-ukraine-energy-grid-causing-power-cuts" /><summary type="html">Russia launched its heaviest combined assault on Ukraine’s energy infrastructure in months on Wednesday, killing seven people and triggering emergency power cuts in Kyiv and nearby regions. The strikes came as officials warned of a difficult winter amid Russian attacks on Ukraine’s power and heating infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump renews calls for former Federal Reserve chief Jerome Powell's resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f9834b2d79039f191702f6f98830b01df91456803b168721c87af71cd0d360c</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T23:44:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-trump-renews-calls-for-former-federal-reserve-chief-jerome-powell-resignation--58eead028846.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-trump-renews-calls-for-former-federal-reserve-chief-jerome-powell-resignation" /><summary type="html">The Federal Reserve's watchdog on Wednesday found no grounds for a criminal referral over a roughly $1 billion cost overrun on renovations to the central bank's Washington buildings, while faulting project oversight. The findings prompted President Donald Trump to renew his call for former Fed chief Jerome Powell to resign.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount takeover of Warner Bros. Discovery clears legal hurdle</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e55b37b0dba8ba01abab02656211c36dc6c37aa3c634eaf8bd1d2f3cb384b23e</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T22:19:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-paramount-takeover-of-warner-bros-discovery-clears-legal-hurdle--68378233ae13.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-paramount-takeover-of-warner-bros-discovery-clears-legal-hurdle" /><summary type="html">A federal judge on Wednesday approved a settlement clearing Paramount’s takeover of Warner Bros. Discovery after 12 US states challenged the deal on antitrust grounds. The agreement includes safeguards for CNN’s editorial independence and requires the merged studio to release at least 30 films a year for its first two years.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Like a 'rollercoaster': passengers describe harrowing flydubai flight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fba72e56be794ded8ed0add6e0de23ad1a1c6ca0418c75e054ddfd16111fcbde</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T21:31:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/like-a-rollercoaster-passengers-describe-harrowing-flydubai-flight--9d7009b2f605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/like-a-rollercoaster-passengers-describe-harrowing-flydubai-flight" /><summary type="html">As flight FZ 1073 from Dubai to Tel Aviv approached the Jordanian border on Wednesday, passengers knew in an instant that something was wrong when the plane began plummeting from the sky in a rapid dive. It was like "we were having very big turbulence, but there was no turbulence", passenger Almog Italie told AFP, describing the sensation of losing thousands of feet of altitude in seconds as similar to riding a "rollercoaster". FRANCE 24's August Hakansson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK PM Burnham reopens divisive debate on rejoining EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f9980db52172c2e51f54d1f438b42dd5a01108519bc4f6088cd9e4ffd26a4dc</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T21:08:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260930-uk-pm-burnham-reopens-divisive-debate-on-rejoining-eu--c4eec8c6baf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260930-uk-pm-burnham-reopens-divisive-debate-on-rejoining-eu" /><summary type="html">Andy Burnham put the idea of Britain rejoining the EU on the table Wednesday, breaking a taboo for a UK prime minister and reopening the divisive Brexit debate. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Catherine Barnard, Professor of European Law at the University of Cambridge, says that Burnham "is sending the message that actually it's been pretty cold being on the outside of the EU so we're now looking at the alternatives".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>UK PM Burnham reopens divisive debate on rejoining EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36b411fc94dd2a8f5c90bf71f12f02c0ab0aef4b41b3178b7ee54d6b4876d5ac</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T20:55:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-reopens-divisive-debate-on-rejoining-eu--23aa3f379bb6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-reopens-divisive-debate-on-rejoining-eu" /><summary type="html">Andy Burnham put the idea of Britain rejoining the EU on the table Wednesday, breaking a taboo for a UK prime minister and reopening the divisive Brexit debate. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Catherine Barnard, Professor of European Law at the University of Cambridge, says that Burnham "is sending the message that actually it's been pretty cold being on the outside of the EU so we're now looking at the alternatives".</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian AI expert, Timnit Gebru, wins 'alternative Nobel'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7811968226731690ba43cda62ba4948f59c18e0b97dc2b9b536216224471b12</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T20:44:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-ai-expert-timnit-gebru-wins-alternative-nobel--fc9f29a4fc4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-ai-expert-timnit-gebru-wins-alternative-nobel" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Africa's richest man breaks ground on a 16 billion dollar oil refinery in Kenya. Also, at universities across Cameroon, programming is overshadowed with uncertainty amidst an indefinite strike by lecturers. And I speak to Ethiopian-born computer scientist and pioneering AI ethicist Timnit Gebru as she is  honored with the Swedish Right Livelihood Award for her work on how AI is influenced by biases.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Hegseth says US cut number of generals, admirals by 20%</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5284230f2607bafae3d6ec712d344165e1baaed67d3ed39f188f983e573d2bf</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T20:16:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260930-hegseth-says-us-cut-number-of-generals-admirals-by-20--b5b38bdefe4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260930-hegseth-says-us-cut-number-of-generals-admirals-by-20" /><summary type="html">Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth announced Wednesday that the United States has slashed the number of its generals and admirals by 20 percent, in a move he said is aimed at "accountability."</summary></entry><entry><title>Meet 'America': Trump’s AI chatbot changes answers after challenging his claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd1e1d3d8011ee717b3f7ceaa7edeb75dd080adb575f41f1ce7fff0320b7db04</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T20:08:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/meet-america-trump-s-ai-chatbot-changes-answers-after-challenging-his-claims-1--7d4ab69afaa6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/meet-america-trump-s-ai-chatbot-changes-answers-after-challenging-his-claims-1" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has launched “America”, an AI chatbot designed as a digital portal for US government information. But its responses appear to be changing. The chatbot initially challenged several of Trump’s claims, including on the 2020 election and inflation, providing evidence and links. More recently, it has refused to answer some of the same questions. Other responses still contradict Trump, while some echo his views. Vedika Bahl tests the chatbot, and its varying answers in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>'Hard to see Man City getting anything other than the book thrown at them', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6d2e075eec65522ab5fc21bfb699179b627a31f836577aac09980f64fa5b025</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:56:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/hard-to-see-man-city-getting-anything-other-than-the-book-thrown-at-them-expert-says--eec4ac67ec8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/hard-to-see-man-city-getting-anything-other-than-the-book-thrown-at-them-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Manchester City enjoyed a meteoric rise from mid-table mediocrity to Premier League domination, but their golden era could be forever tarnished after they were found guilty of scores of financial rule breaches. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with James Reade, Professor of Economics at the University of Reading. He says that it's unlikely that the club will see any leniency from football authorities: "it's hard to see it getting anything other than the book thrown at them".</summary></entry><entry><title>Ronaldo leaves Portugal training camp after coach drops him from upcoming match</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81f7bc062ec55f20314639eb3d06e9212516b5314f13468fdc00edbb30246071</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:14:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20260930-ronaldo-leaves-portugal-training-camp-after-coach-drops-him-from-upcoming-match--008afe162416.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260930-ronaldo-leaves-portugal-training-camp-after-coach-drops-him-from-upcoming-match" /><summary type="html">Portugal captain and striker Cristiano Ronaldo said Wednesday he had walked out on the national team's training camp in Copenhagen after coach Jorge Jesus announced the 41-year-old player would be dropped from the team's next match against Denmark.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Clashes between French teens, police as school blockades intensify</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b93b98c74474b383beb42e188061ae40fe4cbf09aea2ae2c77a89918c0eb031</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:07:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/clashes-between-french-teens-police-as-school-blockades-intensify--c2939a8fc8e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/clashes-between-french-teens-police-as-school-blockades-intensify" /><summary type="html">French teenagers on Tuesday set fire to rubbish bins and threw projectiles at police who responded with batons and tear gas, with hundreds detained across the country over the blockades and protests demanding better conditions at schools. Since last week, students have staged protests outside hundreds of schools over grievances including timetables, class sizes and a shortage of teachers as well as overheated classrooms during this year's heatwaves. FRANCE 24's Rachel Griffiths reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia back to civil war? Horn of Africa fears spillover effect of renewed fighting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4cdb6bd9d14b015841cfb4aed104abe1789c8735fea33910384b532f8784a5c7</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:04:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260930-ethiopia-back-to-civil-war-horn-of-africa-fears-spillover-effect-of-renewed-fighting--2f65ee3843c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260930-ethiopia-back-to-civil-war-horn-of-africa-fears-spillover-effect-of-renewed-fighting" /><summary type="html">After contagion in the Arabian Peninsula, should the entire Horn of Africa fear a domino effect? Just as Donald Trump’s decision to invade Iran drew the Saudis back to Yemen: did threats over the Strait of Bab el-Mandeb light the fuse in Ethiopia, where last week, unresolved issues between the government and its Tigray region erupted? Could a potential return to civil war draw in regional rivals?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>British PM alleges there are 'strong indications' Iran was involved in Fairford airbase incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a875e8e9f914a23fe59ef72588e7ad0d678811f0ac73c1887db19cbc0caf4da2</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:01:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-british-pm-alleges-there-are-strong-indications-iran-was-involved-in-fairford-airbase-incid--08fbaf5d3af6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-british-pm-alleges-there-are-strong-indications-iran-was-involved-in-fairford-airbase-incident" /><summary type="html">UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham on Wednesday insisted that there were "strong indications" that Tehran was involved in a security incident on Sunday near an airbase in England that the US military uses in its war against Iran. The British government has still not explained the nature of the incident – in which five British men were arrested only to be later released on bail – and no explosives were found at the scene.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UK-France 'one in, one out' migrant exchange deal is scrapped</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4820d25dae4948e8d0b6bfa7ddbb4d2b053acf06d59fc6b613c90f669f278b3</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T17:12:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-uk-france-one-in-one-out-migrant-exchange-deal-is-scrapped--b0a81c404ab0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-uk-france-one-in-one-out-migrant-exchange-deal-is-scrapped" /><summary type="html">A British-French agreement aimed at reducing the number of people trying to cross the English Channel in small boats has been scrapped, London said Wednesday. The pilot programme was intended to break the business model of "people smugglers" by exchanging undocumented migrants who had made the crossing for people who legally applied for asylum.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France to unveil 2027 budget as debt hits record high</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7172abc70d552c7d67ebf9b7980f1d9609cc84e6d5caf4dde62df5a2348ea99</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T16:58:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-france-to-unveil-2027-budget-as-debt-hits-record-high--f66186eaa935.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-france-to-unveil-2027-budget-as-debt-hits-record-high" /><summary type="html">As the French government prepares to unveil its latest budget, the country's debt is at a record high and growing every day. France's public debt currently stands at nearly 3.6 trillion euros, nearly 60 billion of that added in the last three months alone.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel PM says pilot of rerouted flight tried to crash plane</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe105611e7100b088b099584a45aa5f713812903c4455be9b951742774cefc6b</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T16:57:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-israel-pm-says-pilot-of-rerouted-flight-tried-to-crash-plane--5cabcaf4d8c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-israel-pm-says-pilot-of-rerouted-flight-tried-to-crash-plane" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Wednesday that the pilot of a Tel Aviv-bound flydubai flight had tried to crash the plane and kill its passengers, after the aircraft was forced to make an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia. Passengers gave a similar account of the incident on board, describing a fight for control after the plane suddenly plummeted, losing around 17,000 feet of altitude in the span of a minute, according to the Flightradar24 website.</summary></entry><entry><title>New York Gov pushes for probe into Cornell's handling of gang rape allegation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc0e183651f3bea31ac686073923e24ccae93dce617bf344744f6cd2d8dbb687</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T16:55:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-new-york-gov-pushes-for-probe-into-cornell-s-handling-of-gang-rape-allegation--be0ab32fac39.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-new-york-gov-pushes-for-probe-into-cornell-s-handling-of-gang-rape-allegation" /><summary type="html">New York Gov. Kathy Hochul on Tuesday called for an investigation into Cornell University's response to a 2024 gang rape allegation in which a woman says she was sexually assaulted by seven students after being plied with alcohol and drugs. It comes as prosecutors reopen an investigation into the alleged rape following claims the elite college failed to properly punish the men involved.</summary></entry><entry><title>Climate change reshaping the polar oceans, says report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:31c86b9004f89491655b92ce663dbc9a40e01e54a2fced1c3b1fe0c1bb5dd405</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T16:53:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-climate-change-reshaping-the-polar-oceans-says-report--cea26863ccb0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-climate-change-reshaping-the-polar-oceans-says-report" /><summary type="html">Climate change is increasingly reshaping the polar oceans, with Arctic waters warming rapidly, sea ice shrinking and wildlife losing habitat at both ends of the planet, an annual report said Wednesday. The Copernicus Ocean State Report depicts profound changes across the world's seas, from record-breaking heatwaves in the Mediterranean and Black seas to shifts in marine ecosystems and increasingly acidic waters.</summary></entry><entry><title>Syria: An exclusive look at the integration of Uyghur fighters in armed forces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88f0d98dad42e3b6f34a0cb58ac2912909324ba54bbeeae045657eee031c0a4d</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T16:45:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-syria-an-exclusive-look-at-the-integration-of-uyghur-fighters-in-armed-forces--7e259938e61f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-syria-an-exclusive-look-at-the-integration-of-uyghur-fighters-in-armed-forces" /><summary type="html">Several factions of foreign fighters are credited with helping topple Syria's Bashar al-Assad nearly two years ago - among them, the Uyghurs, a predominantly Muslim, Turkic ethnic minority spread across Central Asia - notably in China's Xinjiang region. They eventually became amongst the largest contingents of foreign fighters in Syria, though those who have stayed and built lives there are notoriously secretive. However, France 24's Wassim Nasr was recently in Syria and had exclusive access to Uyghur fighters there.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Attempted terror attack’: What happened on board the rerouted Flydubai flight?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:402f23c65e8c02b3005ddc3bc8143594f893ba11ea42b19677b957051997c8ad</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T16:04:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-attempted-terror-attack-what-happened-on-board-the-rerouted-flydubai-flight--427fdbaf19b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-attempted-terror-attack-what-happened-on-board-the-rerouted-flydubai-flight" /><summary type="html">The co-pilot of a flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv ​tried ‌to crash the plane after stabbing the pilot, but passengers then ⁠held him down while other pilots landed the plane safely in Saudi Arabia, Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said ‌on Wednesday.</summary></entry></feed>
